E('democracy', 'Democracy is a system of government in which power belongs to the people.', 'It began in ancient Athens around 508 BC.', 'In a direct democracy, citizens vote on laws themselves.', 'In a representative democracy, citizens elect people to decide for them.', 'Modern democracies usually protect rights like free speech and fair elections.', 'Voting rights were gradually extended to all adults over the 19th and 20th centuries.', 'Winston Churchill joked that it is the worst form of government except all the others.')
E('communism|karl marx|marx|communist manifesto|marxism', 'Communism is a political idea that aims for a classless society where property is owned in common.', 'Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels published The Communist Manifesto in 1848.', 'Marx argued that history is driven by struggle between social classes.', 'He predicted workers would overthrow capitalism.', 'Communist states, like the USSR and China, were run by single parties.', 'Many of them became repressive and suffered economic failures.', 'Marx’s ideas still influence economics, history and sociology.')
E('capitalism', 'Capitalism is an economic system based on private ownership and free markets.', 'It grew in Europe from the 16th century and spread with the Industrial Revolution.', 'Businesses compete to make profits.', 'Prices are mostly set by supply and demand.', 'Adam Smith is often seen as its first great theorist.', 'Most countries today mix capitalism with government regulation and welfare.', 'Supporters credit it with growth and innovation; critics point to inequality.')
E('socialism', 'Socialism is a family of ideas in which the community or state owns or controls key parts of the economy.', 'It developed in the 19th century in response to the Industrial Revolution.', 'Socialists aim to reduce inequality.', 'Democratic socialists seek change through elections.', 'Many European countries combine markets with strong social programs.', 'The word means different things in different countries.')
E('stoicism|stoics|seneca|epictetus', 'Stoicism is an ancient philosophy about living calmly and virtuously.', 'It was founded in Athens by Zeno of Citium around 300 BC.', 'Stoics teach that we should focus only on what we can control.', 'They value wisdom, courage, justice and self-control.', 'Famous Stoics include Seneca, Epictetus and Marcus Aurelius.', 'Epictetus was born enslaved.', 'It has become popular again as a practical guide to resilience.')
E('nietzsche|friedrich nietzsche|god is dead', 'Friedrich Nietzsche was a German philosopher.', 'He lived from 1844 to 1900.', 'He wrote that “God is dead”, meaning traditional religious values were losing their hold.', 'He wrote about the “will to power” and the Übermensch, or “overman”.', 'His books include Thus Spoke Zarathustra.', 'The Nazis misused his ideas, partly through his sister’s editing.', 'He had a mental breakdown in 1889.')
E('descartes|rene descartes|i think therefore i am', 'René Descartes was a French philosopher and mathematician.', 'He lived from 1596 to 1650.', 'He wrote “I think, therefore I am”.', 'He tried to doubt everything to find what was certain.', 'He invented the Cartesian coordinate system used in graphs.', 'He is called the father of modern philosophy.')
E('kant|immanuel kant', 'Immanuel Kant was a German philosopher of the Enlightenment.', 'He lived from 1724 to 1804.', 'He wrote the Critique of Pure Reason.', 'He argued we should act only by rules we could want everyone to follow, the “categorical imperative”.', 'He reportedly walked at the same time every day, so neighbours could set their clocks by him.', 'He never travelled far from his hometown of Königsberg.')
E('machiavelli|the prince|niccolo machiavelli', 'Niccolò Machiavelli was a Florentine diplomat and political writer.', 'He lived from 1469 to 1527.', 'He wrote The Prince, a handbook on gaining and keeping power.', 'He argued rulers sometimes must act ruthlessly.', 'He asked whether it is better to be loved or feared, concluding feared is safer if you cannot be both.', '“Machiavellian” now means cunning and unscrupulous.')
E('christianity|jesus|jesus christ', 'Christianity is a religion based on the life and teachings of Jesus of Nazareth.', 'Jesus lived in the 1st century AD in Roman-ruled Judea and was crucified around AD 30 to 33.', 'Christians believe Jesus is the Son of God and rose from the dead.', 'His teachings stress love, forgiveness and care for the poor.', 'The New Testament tells his story.', 'Christianity spread across the Roman Empire and became its official religion.', 'It is the world’s largest religion, with over two billion followers.')
E('judaism|jewish', 'Judaism is one of the oldest monotheistic religions, the religion of the Jewish people.', 'Its roots go back more than 3,000 years.', 'Its core text is the Torah, the first five books of the Hebrew Bible.', 'It traces back to Abraham and to Moses, who received the law at Mount Sinai.', 'Its holy days include Shabbat, Passover and Yom Kippur.', 'It shaped both Christianity and Islam.')
E('hinduism|hindu', 'Hinduism is a major religion of South Asia, often called the oldest living religion.', 'Its roots go back thousands of years, to the Vedic period.', 'It has no single founder.', 'Key ideas include dharma (duty), karma (action and consequence) and reincarnation.', 'Its sacred texts include the Vedas, the Upanishads and the Bhagavad Gita.', 'It has about 1.2 billion followers.')
E('sikhism|guru nanak', 'Sikhism is a religion founded in the Punjab region of South Asia.', 'It was founded by Guru Nanak, who lived from 1469 to 1539.', 'It teaches belief in one God and the equality of all people.', 'Its holy book is the Guru Granth Sahib.', 'The Golden Temple in Amritsar is its holiest site.', 'Sikh temples serve free meals to all visitors in a langar.')
E('vatican|vatican city|pope', 'Vatican City is the world’s smallest country and the home of the Pope.', 'It became an independent state in 1929.', 'It lies inside Rome.', 'The Pope is the leader of the Catholic Church.', 'It contains St Peter’s Basilica and the Sistine Chapel.', 'It is guarded by the Swiss Guard.')
E('human rights|universal declaration of human rights', 'Human rights are basic rights and freedoms that belong to every person.', 'The UN adopted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights on 10 December 1948.', 'It was drafted by a committee chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt.', 'It includes rights to life, liberty, education and freedom of thought.', 'It is the most translated document in the world.', '10 December is now Human Rights Day.')
E('feminism', 'Feminism is the movement for equal rights and opportunities for women.', 'It is often described in “waves”, starting in the 19th century.', 'The first wave focused on votes and legal rights.', 'The second wave, from the 1960s, focused on work, family and equality.', 'Mary Wollstonecraft wrote A Vindication of the Rights of Woman in 1792.', 'It has transformed laws, workplaces and family life.')
E('philosophy', 'Philosophy is the study of big questions about knowledge, reality, ethics and meaning.', 'In the West it is usually traced to ancient Greece, around the 6th century BC.', 'The word means “love of wisdom”.', 'Major branches include ethics, logic, metaphysics and epistemology.', 'Great traditions also developed in China, India and the Islamic world.', 'Philosophy gave birth to many sciences.')
E('existentialism|sartre|jean-paul sartre|camus|albert camus', 'Existentialism is a philosophy focused on individual freedom, choice and meaning.', 'It flourished in mid-20th-century Europe.', 'Jean-Paul Sartre said “existence precedes essence”: we create our own meaning.', 'Albert Camus wrote about the “absurd”, using the myth of Sisyphus.', 'Simone de Beauvoir applied it to women’s lives in The Second Sex.', 'Its ideas influenced literature, theatre and film.')
E('lao tzu|laozi|taoism|daoism|tao te ching', 'Laozi is the legendary founder of Taoism, a Chinese philosophy and religion.', 'He is traditionally said to have lived in the 6th century BC.', 'He is credited with the Tao Te Ching.', 'Taoism teaches living in harmony with the Tao, “the Way”.', 'It values simplicity, humility and going with the flow of nature.', 'The yin-yang symbol is linked with Taoist thought.')
E('ancient philosophy|presocratics|heraclitus', 'The Presocratic philosophers were the first Greek thinkers to explain nature without myths.', 'They lived in the 6th and 5th centuries BC.', 'Thales thought everything was made of water.', 'Heraclitus said you cannot step in the same river twice.', 'Democritus proposed that everything is made of tiny atoms.', 'They began the tradition of science and philosophy in the West.')
